    {
      "id": "lEQa",
      "code_hash": "f4c2c75f2b5e93e53233004aa0b7dbf5",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"coupling-running-and-the-zero-quartic-limit\">Coupling running and the zero-quartic limit</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The local operators use <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\psi||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\psi Z_m||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\phi||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\phi Z_M||)</marimo-tex>, <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_g Z_\\psi\\sqrt{Z_\\phi}||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\lambda Z_\\phi^2||)</marimo-tex>. Their generated coefficients form a six-by-six system.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The calculation derives <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta_g||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\beta_\\lambda||)</marimo-tex> by differentiating the bare couplings <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mu^\\epsilon gZ_g||)</marimo-tex> and <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\mu^{2\\epsilon}\\lambda Z_\\lambda||)</marimo-tex>. The two theories have equal coupling beta functions but different mass constants. Although <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(Z_\\lambda||)</marimo-tex> contains <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/\\lambda||)</marimo-tex>, the additive shift <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\lambda(Z_\\lambda-1)||)</marimo-tex> stays finite at <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\lambda=0||)</marimo-tex>: Yukawa loops generate a quartic interaction.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
